# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# cad/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with pcb/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# - <filename>: exactly as it appears on disk. A suite going missing
#   (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing unregistered is a
#   loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
# - assertions=N: the suite must report exactly N total assertions
#   (passed+failed). This is what makes `check(true); quit(0)` planted above
#   the real assertions FAIL instead of passing a bare `n_pass > 0` floor.
#   When a suite legitimately grows or shrinks, re-pin here in a deliberate,
#   reviewed own-commit — the same act as registering the suite.
# - real-worker: the suite's Results line must prove real_worker_used=true.
#   No cad suite uses it yet; the runner refuses the attribute until
#   cad/scripts/probe-worker-methods.py exists, because the attribute is a
#   claim about a live worker and an unprobed worker cannot back it.
#
# This file is deliberately NOT named test_*.gd (it must not match the
# runner's own `test_*.gd` glob) and NOT executable GDScript.

# Two controls (a normal middle-drag orbits; a received release stops the
# orbit) plus the repro (a LOST middle-button release must not strand the
# camera in orbit).
test_orbit_camera_stuck.gd assertions=3

# Reference meshes: a GLB built and written by the suite itself is loaded,
# converted from metres/Y-up to millimetres/Z-up with its 0.001 root scale
# composed, posed by the evaluation's 4x4, mounted shaded + outlined, cached
# against a pose change and re-read against a file change; plus path
# resolution, the missing-file report, a units= change being different
# geometry that the record reports (so a cache can key on it), the shared
# feature-edge extractor, reference-aware auto-framing, and a .gltf whose
# external buffer is rewritten under an untouched manifest being re-read.
test_reference_meshes.gd assertions=42

# The GUI "Import mesh…" action: the button and the scene-declared picker
# exist in both layouts, a pick appends exactly one refN = mesh("...") line
# with a path relative to the saved .mcad, the write lands on the SAME
# DocumentBuffer the paired text editor reads (real broker, real buffer), an
# evaluation follows on its own, a second import becomes ref2, and an unsaved
# document gets an absolute path plus an on-screen warning that survives
# Save-As and still resolves. A path containing a line break is refused
# rather than written into a one-line statement.
test_mesh_import.gd assertions=37

# Measuring a foreign mesh: a CSG plate with two plain through holes, one hole
# 1.9 mm from the outline, one drilled 30 degrees off the plate normal, a blind
# pocket and a convex boss, baked in-test and posed by a non-identity
# transform. Pins the propose half (segmentation, plane and cylinder fits,
# facet count, the inscribed-vs-circumscribed distinction, the axis of the
# tilted hole) and the verify half (colliders, refined centres in both frames,
# the pin that actually fits, through vs blind, a too-large gauge reporting
# contacts, the boss verifying while an oversize and an in-mid-air boss
# candidate do not, a gauge buried in solid material refusing to fit, a
# clearance searched to the part's own extent rather than to a multiple of
# the pin, a gauge in open space reporting the search bound as a FLOOR and not
# as a clearance, a mirrored copy and an inward-wound copy each keeping the
# sense of every feature, a pixel-less probe, and the ray-grid fallback's
# limits). Plus two plate stacks sharing a face: the coincident triangles are
# two crossings, so a pin in open air beyond them still fits. Also that two
# concurrent requests for one file segment it once and both get the answer,
# and that reference scoping holds past Godot's 32 collision layers: a
# blocker sharing the target's final layer is excluded under the target's
# mask, and the SAME job under every layer (name still attached) is shrunk
# by that blocker, so the mask is the scope and the name alone scopes nothing.
test_mesh_measurement.gd assertions=72

# The measurement VERBS through PanelTools.handle, on a two-plate stack with
# one pair of drills through both plates and a boss on top, posed by a
# non-identity transform. Pins the envelope an agent depends on rather than
# the physics: success/units on every reply, one row per drill naming every
# node it crosses, every position and axis in world AND local millimetres with
# the fit residual carried through, the boss found as convex, the gauge verb's
# fits/contacts, a probe hit attributed to its node, per-pane scales from
# view_overlay, and a named error — never an empty result — for an unmounted
# reference, an unsupported gauge shape, a pixel-less probe, an unknown
# overlay mode and a node= filter that matches nothing. Also that a second
# reference running down the drill cannot change a measurement scoped to
# this one while an UNSCOPED call does see it, that a node= filter is a match
# when any one mounted reference carries it, that a diameter limit is a world
# millimetre under a scaled pose, and that a pose scaled by 2 reports twice
# the diameter in world and the file's own in local. Also that a reference
# set which keeps changing while a verb waits comes back marked stale with a
# reason, and a settled one does not.
test_measurement_verbs.gd assertions=35

# Failure and size handling for references: a truncated GLB, a text file
# wearing a .glb extension, a missing file, an unreadable format and an
# unresolvable relative path all mounted in ONE evaluation next to a good
# reference. Pins the status taxonomy and the reason naming the file, the
# wireframe marker drawn at the failed reference's own pose, the good
# reference and the rest of the scene surviving all four, the marker clearing
# on the next good evaluation, the three size ceilings (bytes refused before
# the parse, triangles refused after it, the outline budget degrading to
# shaded-only) with the measured numbers in the messages, and
# minerva_cad_references carrying references[i].status and its reason.
test_reference_failures.gd assertions=30

# Pointing at a reference: a two-box GLB built in-test, declared mm/Z-up so the
# frame conversion is the identity and the suite is about WHICH node was hit.
# Pins the node inventory keyed by PATH (two branches each hold a node
# called "Body") and the scene-declared sidebar rows, a click in the
# top pane picking the nearer of two bodies and reporting its surface point in
# both frames, the MCP readback (get_selected_reference / select_reference,
# including a miss being an error and a flat face reporting no hole), the
# cad/point anchor validating, resolving, moving with a re-posed reference by
# the projected pixel displacement, the click normal being stored in the
# reference's own frame and turning only when the pose turns it, and going
# stale — not crashing — when the
# reference leaves the document, and the two selections coexisting: the picker
# is a plain Node that only ever sees input the edge overlay did not take.
# Also the annotation-tool status hook: an armed tool with nothing selected
# gets an actionable warning, a selection clears it, and an MCP selection
# fires annotation_tool_status_changed so the host re-reads the hook.
test_reference_selection.gd assertions=49

# Save-to-note and back: the real panel scene is set up, saved as a
# plugin_data note, freed the way closing a tab frees it, and a second,
# untouched panel is restored from the note through the JSON wrapper the host
# actually writes. Pins the payload (schema, version, source, path, per-pane
# cameras, the mesh() specs) and that every value in it is JSON-native, the
# reopened tab's source, path, per-pane camera preset and mounted reference
# geometry read off the live scene graph, the second camera application that
# survives an evaluation's auto-frame, the refusals (wrong version, foreign
# schema, malformed source) leaving the open document alone, and
# render_for_llm returning an image part plus one text part naming every
# reference with its status and bounds — including a document with none.
test_cad_note.gd assertions=40

# Interference between the evaluated solid and a reference: a CSG board posed
# by a non-identity transform, and four solids built in-test and handed over as
# worker mesh data. Pins the solid's collider being rebuilt on every
# evaluation and never cached, a boss driven clean through the board reporting
# the right node with a crossing on the boss circle at a board face to 0.05 mm,
# both frames agreeing under the pose, the penetration coming back as the
# board's own thickness, the same boss lifted 0.1 mm reporting a clean zero
# (with the previous points gone), a 0.2 mm sliver overlap with NO vertex of
# either body inside the other still being reported, a cube buried in the
# board being caught by parity alone, the status line naming the first
# offender, and the reference=/node= scoping (a filter matching nothing
# reports nothing). 24 assertions = 2 fixture + 5 collider + 8 through +
# 3 clear + 2 sliver + 2 buried + 2 scope.
test_interference.gd assertions=24

# Clearance between the evaluated solid and a reference: two bars crossing at
# right angles with 0.8 mm of air between them, where every vertex of either
# bar is more than 60 mm from the other, so the gap is face-to-face and a
# vertex-sampling check cannot find it. The exact distance runs in the worker
# (pinned by worker/tests/test_clearance.py); this suite pins everything the
# PANEL owns, against a stand-in backend that derives its answer from the blob
# the module actually wrote: the request naming geometry by hash and fitting
# the host's 64 KiB IPC cap, the upload-on-miss retry, content-addressed blob
# files that decode to the POSED world geometry, the sweep of blobs nothing
# references, an unchanged reference being named rather than re-sent, the
# answer's both-frame points and closest-first order, the mandatory
# tessellation tolerance and the status line quoting it, pass at 0.5 and a
# fail at 1.0 naming the node, node= scoping the question before it is asked,
# a zero-gap pair carrying the interference flag and no points, and four
# refusals (no required_mm, a node filter matching nothing, a worker error
# quoted verbatim, and a refused check reporting no pairs).
# 24 assertions = 2 fixture + 8 upload + 10 answer + 4 refusal.
test_clearance.gd assertions=24
